# Coding conventions

## Naming

- Name functions by purpose, not implementation (`getActiveUsers`, not `filterArrayByFlag`).

## Folders and files

- Folders: camelCase, except component folders = PascalCase (`Card/`).
- Files: components = PascalCase, helpers/types = camelCase.
- Component-related files are prefixed with the component name: `Card.jsx`, `Card.css` (never `cardStyle.css`), `Card.types.js`, `Card.constants.js`, `Card.test.jsx`, `Card.fixtures.js`.
- Constants → `Card.constants.js`. Custom types → `Card.types.js`. Plain `constants.js` / `types.js` only when shared across components in a folder.
- Enums live in `*.constants.js` — they produce runtime values.

## Helpers

- Helpers are pure functions (this project uses `helpers/`, not `utils/`).
- 3 or fewer → `Card.helpers.js` (or colocated under the component folder).
- 4 or more → a `helpers/` folder, one function per file named after the function, with a colocated test:

```text
helpers/
  formatPrice.js
  formatPrice.test.js
```

## Hooks and components

- Hooks: file named after the hook (`useCardFocus.js`), in a `hooks/` folder.
- Components: one folder per component. Nest its `helpers/`, `hooks/`, and any subcomponents inside that folder; only lift shared code up to a common ancestor once more than one component needs it — shared subcomponents go in `common/`.

## Logic vs UI

- JSX renders and wires clicks. Filtering, sorting, matching, formatting, and chart math go in **pure helpers** (with tests). Homey fetch/subscribe/setCapability lives in **hooks**.
- Do not put Homey `runFlowCardAction` / `setCapabilityValue` inline in a large render tree — a small named function or hook is enough.
- Split a component when a chunk has its own state, a clear name (`SpeakerRow`, `RoomTemperature`), or a second caller. Do not split one-off markup into files “for cleanliness”.
- Do not split on line count alone. Do split when one file mixes unrelated concerns (e.g. SVG chart geometry + room chrome).
- Prefer a local function in the same file until a second caller exists. `common/` only after two parents need it.
